nla_reliability — third-party attribution
=========================================

This work builds on **Natural Language Autoencoders (NLA)** introduced by
Anthropic / Transformer Circuits.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NLA method (architecture, training protocol, AV / AR pair)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fraser-Taliente, Kantamneni, Ong, et al.,
"Natural Language Autoencoders Produce Unsupervised Explanations of LLM
Activations", Transformer Circuits, 2026.

  Paper:          https://transformer-circuits.pub/2026/nla/index.html
  Research post:  https://www.anthropic.com/research/natural-language-autoencoders

This repository does not retrain, fine-tune, or modify NLAs. It consumes
pretrained Anthropic NLA checkpoints (below) as black boxes and adds a
reliability evaluation layer on top (mean-centered cosines, MPNet text
consistency, G-theory variance decomposition, linear probes, synthesis
figures/tables).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pretrained NLA checkpoints (used unchanged)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The AV and AR checkpoints below are Anthropic-released Gemma-3-12B layer-32
NLAs, distributed via the kitft account on Hugging Face Hub.

  AV (activation verbalizer)     kitft/nla-gemma3-12b-L32-av
                                 https://huggingface.co/kitft/nla-gemma3-12b-L32-av
                                 Used by `sample_descriptions.py` (Modal Step 2).

  AR (activation reconstructor)  kitft/nla-gemma3-12b-L32-ar
                                 https://huggingface.co/kitft/nla-gemma3-12b-L32-ar
                                 Used by `reconstruct_scores.py` (Modal Step 3).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored inference client
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
`nla/nla_inference.py` is vendored verbatim (subject to minor local diffs)
from kitft's open-source reimplementation of the Anthropic NLA inference
protocol. It is licensed under MIT by kitft.

  Source:        https://github.com/kitft/natural_language_autoencoders
  Upstream file: https://github.com/kitft/natural_language_autoencoders/blob/main/nla_inference.py

The file provides BOTH halves of the NLA pair:

  * `NLAClient`  — AV / activation verbalization via SGLang `input_embeds`.
                   Used by this repo in `sample_descriptions.py` (Step 2).
  * `NLACritic` — AR / activation reconstruction (pure torch, no SGLang).
                   Used by this repo in `reconstruct_scores.py` (Step 3).

See `nla/ATTRIBUTION.md` for per-file vendoring details.

